  "title": "How ‘F1 The Movie’ took a page from the ‘Barbie’ marketing playbook",
  "summary": "These days, did a movie even come out if it wasn’t embedded in every corner of culture? Apple’s marketing for F1: The Movie echoed the immersive frenzy of Barbie—from out‑of‑home visuals and surprise Brad Pitt appearances to personalized iPhone push notifications. The campaign turned the film into a cultural event, uniting F1 fans and mainstream audiences months before opening.",
